# Defect 231, panel 190's R3 and the one shape it exempts (2026-10-04). A
# function with two or more ways out leaves by one exit (`ir/exits.hero`),
# and one the pass cannot merge is refused by the verifier, never left with
# a sweep in every returning block in silence. A hole is the one way a
# function with a result falls off its end: the checker holds
# `missing_return` back in a module with a hole (spec § 12), lowering writes
# that edge as a `return` with no value, and the pass leaves the function as
# lowering made it. No binary is made of such a program, and the verifier
# names this shape as its one exemption, so the dump below still ends with
# the holes. Measured with the exemption removed, the same day: `--dump-ir`
# and `build` both exit 2 here, *the lowered program is not well formed*.
#
# `capped` falls off its end and keeps both of its returns; `scaled`, in the
# same program, has two ways out and leaves by one exit.

function capped(n: i64) -> i64
    if n > 10
        return 10
    _ = ???

function scaled(n: i64) -> i64
    if n > 10
        return n * 2
    return n

function main()
    print(capped(3), scaled(4))
